### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to create a card that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container ----------
   Keeps the perspective so the rotation looks 3D */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
    perspective: 800px;          /* How far the viewer is from the card */
}

/* ---------- Card ----------
   The element that actually rotates */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d; /* Needed for 3D children */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* Smooth animation */
    cursor: pointer;
}

/* ---------- Front & Back Faces ----------
   Both faces occupy the same space but are positioned differently */
.front,
.back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden; /* Hide the backside when it's turned away */
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
}

.back {
    background: #4a90e2;
    color: #fff;
    transform: rotateY(180deg); /* Start rotated so we see the front first */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
}

/* ---------- Hover Effect ----------
   Rotate the whole card 180° on hover */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front Face -->
        <div class="front">
            <p>Front Side</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back Face -->
        <div class="back">
            <p>Back Side</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets the 3D perspective (`perspective: 800px`). |
| `.card` | Holds both faces, uses `transform-style: preserve-3d` so child elements keep their 3D positioning. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each face is absolutely positioned on top of each other. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that is turned away. |
| `.back` | Initially rotated 180° so only the front is visible. |
| `.card:hover` | Rotates the entire card 180° around the Y‑axis. |

#### Customization tips

- **Change the rotation axis** – replace `rotateY(180deg)` with `rotateX(180deg)` or `rotateZ(180deg)` for different effects.
- **Add more content** – put images, icons, or text inside the `.front` and `.back` divs.
- **Adjust speed** – modify `transition: transform 0.6s ease;` to make the flip faster or slower.
- **Add shadows or gradients** – style the faces with CSS gradients or additional box‑shadows for depth.

Enjoy experimenting!
